#: docs/display-protocol.rst:2
msgid "Display protocol"
msgstr "显示信息协议"

#: docs/display-protocol.rst:6
msgid ""
"A program that draws knows nothing about the screen its output ends up on: whether it is a color "
"LCD or sixteen levels of gray on e-ink, how much of the color spectrum it covers, how bright it "
"can go, how many physical pixels a cell has and how often it refreshes. Each of these changes "
"what the best rendering is, from the choice of a palette and a dithering strategy to whether "
"animation is worth doing at all. The display protocol lets a program ask, and be told when the "
"answer changes, for example because the window was moved to another screen. It is an open "
"terminal extension in the manner of the other kitty protocols: small, unobtrusive, easy to "
"implement, and no change to what the TTY is."
msgstr ""
"绘图程序通常不了解输出最终到达的屏幕：彩色 LCD "
"还是十六级灰度电子墨水屏、覆盖多少色域、亮度有多高、每个字符单元有多少物理像素、以什么频率刷新。这些都会影响最佳渲染方式，从调色板和抖动策略，到是否值得运行动画。显示信息协议让程序查询这些信息，并在答案变化时收到通知，例如窗口被移到另一块屏幕。它与其他"
" kitty 协议一样，是小巧、低干扰、易于实现的开放终端扩展，不改变 TTY 的本质。"

#: docs/display-protocol.rst:18
msgid "Framing"
msgstr "消息封装"

#: docs/display-protocol.rst:20
msgid "Frames are ``OSC 777`` with the ``display`` selector::"
msgstr "帧使用带有 ``display`` 选择器的 ``OSC 777``：::"

#: docs/display-protocol.rst:24
msgid ""
"They follow the rules every OSC 777 extension shares, which :doc:`extension-framing` gives: the "
"syntax of the fields, which frames are rejected, the units and the clock. The values in the "
"terminal's reports are words, or decimal numbers that may have a fraction, such as "
"``headroom=1.5``, with no leading ``+``. ``v``, the protocol version, is ``1``, and ``op`` is one"
" of ``query``, ``cap``, ``mode`` and ``event``."
msgstr ""
"帧遵循 :doc:`extension-framing` 规定的 OSC 777 共用规则：字段语法、拒绝哪些帧、单位和时钟。终端报告中的值为单词，或可带小数、不带前导 ``+`` "
"的十进制数，例如 ``headroom=1.5``。协议版本 ``v`` 为 ``1``，``op`` 为 ``query``、``cap``、``mode`` 或 ``event``。"

#: docs/display-protocol.rst:32
msgid "Query"
msgstr "查询"

#: docs/display-protocol.rst:34
msgid "A program asks about the display its window is on::"
msgstr "程序查询窗口所在的显示器：::"

#: docs/display-protocol.rst:38
msgid ""
"``id`` is a non-negative 31 bit integer of the program's choosing, echoed in the reply so replies"
" can be matched to queries. A supporting terminal answers::"
msgstr "``id`` 是程序自行选择的非负 31 位整数，回复原样返回，以便匹配查询。支持协议的终端回答：::"

#: docs/display-protocol.rst:44
msgid ""
"A terminal that does not support the protocol ignores the query, so a program must time out and "
"fall back to assuming an ordinary color display."
msgstr "不支持本协议的终端会忽略查询，因此程序必须设置超时，并回退为假定普通彩色显示器。"

#: docs/display-protocol.rst:47
msgid "The fields of the reply are:"
msgstr "回复字段如下："

#: docs/display-protocol.rst:49
msgid "``mode``"
msgstr "``mode``"

#: docs/display-protocol.rst:50
msgid "The current state of the mode described below, ``0`` or ``1``."
msgstr "下述模式的当前状态，``0`` 或 ``1``。"

#: docs/display-protocol.rst:52
msgid "``kind``"
msgstr "``kind``"

#: docs/display-protocol.rst:53
msgid ""
"One of ``lcd``, ``oled``, ``eink`` and ``unknown``. On e-ink, updates are slow and leave ghosts, "
"so a program avoids animation and smooth scrolling and redraws in large, infrequent steps."
msgstr "``lcd``、``oled``、``eink`` 或 ``unknown``。电子墨水屏更新较慢且会残影，因此程序应避免动画和平滑滚动，采用低频、大步幅重绘。"

#: docs/display-protocol.rst:57
msgid "``color``"
msgstr "``color``"

#: docs/display-protocol.rst:58
msgid "One of ``rgb``, ``gray`` and ``mono``."
msgstr "``rgb``、``gray`` 或 ``mono``。"

#: docs/display-protocol.rst:60
msgid "``bits``"
msgstr "``bits``"

#: docs/display-protocol.rst:61
msgid ""
"Bits per color channel, ``0`` when unknown. Sixteen levels of gray are ``color=gray : bits=4``. "
"Together with ``color`` this is what a program needs to choose a palette and whether and how to "
"dither; antialiasing works fine with a few levels and is not what this field decides."
msgstr ""
"每个颜色通道的位数，未知时为 ``0``。十六级灰度表示为 ``color=gray : bits=4``。该字段与 ``color`` "
"一起供程序选择调色板，并决定是否以及如何抖动；少量灰度级也可进行良好的抗锯齿，此字段不决定抗锯齿策略。"

#: docs/display-protocol.rst:66
msgid "``gamut``"
msgstr "``gamut``"

#: docs/display-protocol.rst:67
msgid "One of ``srgb``, ``p3``, ``rec2020`` and ``unknown``: the widest color space the display covers."
msgstr "``srgb``、``p3``、``rec2020`` 或 ``unknown``，表示显示器覆盖的最宽色彩空间。"

#: docs/display-protocol.rst:70
msgid "``headroom``"
msgstr "``headroom``"

#: docs/display-protocol.rst:71
msgid ""
"How much brighter than the white of normal text the terminal can show, as a multiple: ``1`` when "
"there is no extra brightness. See the HDR brightness protocol for how to use it."
msgstr "终端可显示亮度相对于普通文本白色的倍数；没有额外亮度时为 ``1``。使用方式见 HDR 亮度协议。"

#: docs/display-protocol.rst:75
msgid "``scale``"
msgstr "``scale``"

#. Translated reference labels preserve the original explicit section targets.
#: docs/display-protocol.rst:76
msgid ""
"The scaling of the framebuffer that the system asks applications for: how many physical pixels it"
" wants used for one of its own logical units, ``2`` on most high density displays and often a "
"fraction such as ``1.25`` or ``1.5`` on others. ``0`` when unknown. See `Pixels`_ for what it is "
"for."
msgstr ""
"系统要求应用使用的帧缓冲区缩放比例：一个系统逻辑单位需要多少物理像素。多数高密度显示器为 ``2``，其他显示器常用 ``1.25`` 或 ``1.5`` 等小数。未知时为 ``0``。用途见 "
"`像素 <Pixels_>`_。 #noqa"

#: docs/display-protocol.rst:82
msgid "``period``"
msgstr "``period``"

#: docs/display-protocol.rst:83
msgid "The refresh period of the display in microseconds, ``0`` when unknown."
msgstr "显示器刷新周期，单位微秒，未知时为 ``0``。"

#: docs/display-protocol.rst:85
msgid "``ppi``"
msgstr "``ppi``"

#: docs/display-protocol.rst:86
msgid ""
"Physical pixels per inch: how many of the pixels a program draws in fit in an inch of the screen,"
" so that it can draw at a true size. ``0`` when unknown."
msgstr "每英寸的物理像素数：程序绘制的多少像素对应屏幕上一英寸，供程序按真实尺寸绘制。未知时为 ``0``。"

msgid "``appearance``"
msgstr "``appearance``"

msgid "The desktop appearance preference of the host running the terminal. Values are ``light``, ``dark``, and ``no_preference``. The last value also covers desktops that do not expose a preference. This field is independent of the terminal's configured theme and the pane's background. Clients can treat a missing or unrecognized value as ``no_preference``. On Kylin's UKUI desktop, Silkie can also read the UKUI style and MATE GTK theme when a desktop portal preference is unavailable."
msgstr "运行终端的主机的桌面外观偏好。取值为 ``light``（浅色）、``dark``（深色）或 ``no_preference``（无偏好）。该字段独立于终端的配色主题和窗格背景。客户端可以将缺失或无法识别的值视为 ``no_preference``。在麒麟的 UKUI 桌面上，如果门户未提供偏好，Silkie 也可以读取 UKUI 样式和 MATE GTK 主题。"

msgid "In :opt:`high_contrast` ``auto``, the value is ``1`` on e-paper or when macOS Increase Contrast or the Linux desktop requests higher contrast. Linux uses the XDG Settings portal and recognizes high-contrast GTK themes on UKUI. Explicit ``off`` and ``on`` report ``0`` and ``1``. Clients can treat a missing or unrecognized value as ``0``."
msgstr "将 :opt:`high_contrast` 设为 ``auto`` 时，如果显示器为电子纸、macOS 启用了「增强对比度」或 Linux 桌面要求更高对比度，取值为 ``1``。Linux 使用 XDG Settings 门户，也可识别 UKUI 上的高对比度 GTK 主题。``off`` 和 ``on`` 分别强制报告 ``0`` 和 ``1``。客户端可将缺失或无法识别的值视为 ``0``。"

msgid "In :opt:`differentiate_without_color` ``auto``, the value is ``1`` on grayscale and monochrome displays or when macOS Differentiate Without Color is enabled. Explicit ``off`` and ``on`` report ``0`` and ``1``. Clients can treat a missing or unrecognized value as ``0``."
msgstr "将 :opt:`differentiate_without_color` 设为 ``auto`` 时，如果显示器为灰度或黑白，或 macOS 启用了「不用颜色区分」，取值为 ``1``。``off`` 和 ``on`` 分别强制报告 ``0`` 和 ``1``。客户端可将缺失或无法识别的值视为 ``0``。"

#: docs/display-protocol.rst:90
msgid ""
"Values the terminal cannot determine are ``unknown`` or ``0``, never guessed. A terminal that "
"knows nothing about its display, a multiplexer that is not attached, for example, answers with "
"every field unknown and the program is no worse off than before it asked."
msgstr "终端无法确定的值为 ``unknown`` 或 ``0``，绝不猜测。例如未连接客户端的多路复用器，若不了解显示器，所有字段均回答未知，程序的处境不会比查询前更差。"

#: docs/display-protocol.rst:96
msgid "Pixels"
msgstr "像素"

#: docs/display-protocol.rst:98
msgid ""
"A pixel, in this protocol and in every other one of this terminal that measures in pixels (the "
"size of the window and of a cell, the size and placement of an image, the position of a pointer, "
"a pen or a finger, the distance of a scroll), is a physical pixel: one pixel of the framebuffer "
"the terminal draws into. Nothing is expressed in the logical units of the system, which stand for"
" ``scale`` pixels each, and the terminal never stretches what a program draws to make up the "
"difference. A line a program draws one pixel wide is therefore one pixel wide, not a soft blob "
"spread over several, and a program gets every pixel the display has."
msgstr ""
"本协议及终端所有以像素度量的协议（窗口和字符单元尺寸、图像尺寸和放置、指针／笔／手指位置、滚动距离）均使用物理像素，即终端绘制的帧缓冲区中的一个像素。不使用系统逻辑单位（每个逻辑单位对应 "
"``scale`` 个像素），终端也不会拉伸程序绘制的内容来弥补差异。因此，程序绘制的一像素宽直线就是一像素，而非扩散到多个像素的模糊斑块，程序能使用显示器提供的每一个像素。"

#: docs/display-protocol.rst:108
msgid ""
"``scale`` is what the system would have had an application do: the size it wants things drawn at "
"for them to look the size the user chose. A program uses it to decide how big to draw, a rule "
"that is one logical unit thick as ``scale`` pixels for example, and never to convert a position "
"or a size, which are in physical pixels already. ``ppi`` relates those same pixels to the screen "
"itself."
msgstr ""
"``scale`` 表示系统希望应用采用的尺寸，使内容看起来符合用户选择的大小。程序用它决定绘制多大，例如将一个逻辑单位粗的标尺绘制为 ``scale`` "
"像素；不要用它换算已经以物理像素表示的位置或尺寸。``ppi`` 则把这些像素与屏幕的实际尺寸联系起来。"

#: docs/display-protocol.rst:116
msgid "Mode"
msgstr "模式"

#: docs/display-protocol.rst:118
msgid "A program that wants to be told about changes turns them on per terminal window with::"
msgstr "程序可按终端窗口开启变化通知：::"

#: docs/display-protocol.rst:123
msgid ""
"and off with ``mode=0``. The mode is local to the window and is reset by ``RIS``. Programs must "
"turn it off when they exit, suspend or fail, and turn it back on when resumed. Multiplexers keep "
"it with the rest of the terminal state and turn it off when detaching. A terminal may let its "
"user refuse the mode, for every program or for some. A refused mode reads back as off and nothing"
" is reported, so a program reads the mode back rather than assume it was granted."
msgstr ""
"用 ``mode=0`` 关闭。模式仅作用于当前窗口，并由 ``RIS`` "
"重置。程序必须在退出、挂起或失败时关闭，恢复时重新开启。多路复用器与其他终端状态一起保存它，并在脱离连接时关闭。终端可允许用户针对全部或部分程序拒绝模式；被拒绝时读回为关闭，不产生任何报告，因此程序应读回状态，而不是假定已获准。"

#: docs/display-protocol.rst:131
msgid ""
"A ``mode`` request without a ``mode`` field reads the state instead of changing it, and is "
"answered with::"
msgstr "不带 ``mode`` 字段的 ``mode`` 请求读取状态而不修改，回复为：::"

#: docs/display-protocol.rst:136
msgid ""
"A program resuming after a reconnection reads the mode to learn whether it survived, rather than "
"assuming it did."
msgstr "程序重连后恢复时，应读回模式，确认是否仍然有效，而非假定状态保留。"

#: docs/display-protocol.rst:140
msgid "Events"
msgstr "事件"

#: docs/display-protocol.rst:142
msgid ""
"Turning the mode on sends one event with the current values, so a program needs no separate "
"query. After that, while the mode is on, the terminal sends one event whenever any field changes:"
" the window was moved to a display with a different scale or refresh rate, the display's "
"brightness setting changed the headroom, its color profile was switched, or a desktop "
"appearance or accessibility preference changed::"
msgstr "开启模式会先发送一次包含当前值的事件，无需单独查询。此后，只要模式开启，任何字段变化都会产生一条事件：窗口移到缩放比例或刷新率不同的显示器、显示亮度设置改变了亮度余量、切换了色彩配置文件，或桌面外观或辅助功能偏好发生变化。 ::"

#: docs/display-protocol.rst:150
msgid ""
"The fields are those of the ``cap`` reply, without ``id`` and ``mode``, and ``t``, the time the "
"terminal learnt of the change, in milliseconds on the clock the terminal uses for every "
"extension, see :doc:`extension-framing`. Changes are relative to the last event sent, so turning "
"the mode off and on again reports the current values once and then only changes. A change can be "
"reported a short while after it happens, and a program that has turned the mode off may still "
"receive an event that was already on its way. An event is never merged with another or dropped, "
"by the terminal or by a relay."
msgstr ""
"字段与 ``cap`` 回复相同，但不含 ``id`` 和 ``mode``，并带有 ``t``，表示终端获知变化的时刻，以全部扩展共用时钟上的毫秒表示，见 :doc:`extension-"
"framing`。变化相对于上次事件计算，因此关闭再开启模式会报告一次当前值，此后仅报告变化。变化可能稍后才报告，程序关闭模式后仍可能收到已经在途的事件。终端和中继绝不合并或丢弃事件。"

msgid ""
"When ``appearance``, ``high_contrast``, or ``differentiate_without_color`` changes, Silkie sends "
"``SIGWINCH`` to the foreground process group of each affected pane. Programs that enabled "
"in-band resize reports also receive a resize report with the current dimensions. Both "
"notifications work without display mode, so a program can reissue the display query after a "
"resize notification."
msgstr ""
"``appearance``、``high_contrast`` 或 ``differentiate_without_color`` 变化时，"
"Silkie 向每个受影响窗格的前台进程组发送 ``SIGWINCH``。"
"启用带内尺寸报告的程序还会收到一条包含当前尺寸的报告。这两种通知都无需开启显示报告模式，"
"因此程序可以在收到尺寸变化通知后重新查询显示信息。"

#: docs/display-protocol.rst:160
msgid "Relays and multiplexers"
msgstr "中继与多路复用器"

#: docs/display-protocol.rst:162
msgid ""
"A relay such as a mosh-like client, that draws the terminal's screen on a display of its own, "
"answers queries for the display it has, since the terminal at the far end cannot know it. When "
"the relay reconnects to a different client it sends one event to every window with the mode on, "
"so a program that laid out its output for a phone can redo it for a desktop, and the other way "
"round."
msgstr ""
"类似 mosh "
"客户端、将终端画面绘制到自己显示器的中继，应使用自身显示器回答查询，因为远端终端无法得知这些信息。中继重连到不同客户端时，会向每个开启模式的窗口发送一次事件，使原本按手机布局的程序能改为桌面布局，反之亦然。"

#: docs/display-protocol.rst:169
msgid ""
"A multiplexer answers for the display of the client it is attached to, with every field unknown "
"while detached, and sends an event when attached to a client with a different display."
msgstr "多路复用器根据所连接客户端的显示器回答；脱离连接时所有字段为未知，连接到不同显示器的客户端时发送事件。"

#: docs/display-protocol.rst:174
msgid "Configuration"
msgstr "配置"

#: docs/display-protocol.rst:176
msgid ""
"The operating system reports most of these values, but not all. Nothing tells a terminal that it "
"is on e-ink. In Silkie, :opt:`eink_mode` declares an e-paper display and selects black text on "
"white unless a light or dark color scheme was explicitly chosen. It takes precedence over "
"detected display kind and over ``display_info kind=...``. Runtime changes with ``set_eink_mode`` "
"notify display subscribers immediately. The :opt:`display_info` option declares individual "
"properties that the OS cannot, overriding detection; using only ``display_info kind=eink`` "
"changes the report without changing colors. Neither setting guesses whether an e-paper panel is "
"grayscale or color. Currently, Silkie reports ``kind`` only on macOS, and ``gamut`` on macOS and "
"on Wayland compositors that implement the color management protocol. There the compositor gives "
"the primaries of the display, and ``gamut`` is the widest of the three whose area in the CIE 1931"
" chromaticity diagram the display covers at least nine tenths of, ``srgb`` when it covers neither"
" of the wider two. ``headroom`` is the headroom of the :doc:`hdr-protocol`, after the cap of "
":opt:`hdr_max_headroom`, so it is ``1`` unless :opt:`hdr` is enabled and the window is actually "
"showing HDR, which that page says when to expect on macOS and on Wayland."
msgstr ""
"操作系统能报告多数属性，但并非全部；例如没有信息直接告诉终端它位于电子墨水屏上。在 Silkie 中，:opt:`eink_mode` "
"声明电子纸显示器，并在未明确选择浅色或深色配色时启用白底黑字。它优先于检测到的显示器类型和 ``display_info kind=...``。运行时用 ``set_eink_mode`` "
"切换会立即通知显示信息订阅者。:opt:`display_info` 可声明操作系统无法提供的个别属性，并覆盖检测；仅设置 ``display_info kind=eink`` "
"会改变报告而不改变颜色。两种设置都不猜测电子纸是灰度还是彩色。目前 Silkie 仅在 macOS 上报告 ``kind``，在 macOS 及实现色彩管理协议的 Wayland 合成器上报告 "
"``gamut``。后者由合成器提供显示器基色，``gamut`` 选择显示器在 CIE 1931 色度图上覆盖面积至少十分之九的最宽色域；两种较宽色域均未达到时为 "
"``srgb``。``headroom`` 是 :doc:`hdr-protocol` 的亮度余量，已应用 :opt:`hdr_max_headroom` 上限；除非启用 :opt:`hdr` "
"且窗口实际显示 HDR，否则为 ``1``。macOS 和 Wayland 何时可使用 HDR 见该页。"

#: docs/display-protocol.rst:194
msgid ""
"``scale`` is the scale the window system gives the window: the backing scale factor on macOS, the"
" preferred scale of the surface on Wayland, fractional where the compositor says so, and the "
"scale of the desktop taken from ``Xft.dpi`` on X11. On X11, and on Wayland with a compositor that"
" states its fractional scale, the pixels Silkie draws are the pixels of the panel. On macOS they "
"are those of the framebuffer the system keeps for the display, which are the panel's own at the "
"default resolution. At one of the scaled resolutions (*More Space* and its neighbours in the "
"display settings) the system resamples that framebuffer onto the panel, as a Wayland compositor "
"does for a window it could only give a whole number scale. A pixel Silkie draws is then not "
"exactly a pixel of the panel, which no application can avoid, and on macOS ``ppi`` counts the "
"pixels Silkie draws."
msgstr ""
"``scale`` 是窗口系统提供给窗口的比例：macOS 的 backing scale factor、Wayland 表面的首选比例（合成器支持时可为小数），以及 X11 从 "
"``Xft.dpi`` 取得的桌面比例。在 X11 和能声明小数比例的 Wayland 合成器上，Silkie 绘制的像素对应面板像素。在 macOS "
"上，它们是系统为显示器保存的帧缓冲区像素，默认分辨率下对应面板原生像素。选择缩放分辨率（显示设置中的“更多空间”及相邻选项）时，系统会将帧缓冲区重采样到面板，类似 Wayland "
"合成器对只能提供整数缩放比例的窗口所做的处理。这时 Silkie 的像素不再严格对应面板像素，任何应用都无法避免；macOS 上的 ``ppi`` 统计的是 Silkie 绘制的像素。"

#: docs/display-protocol.rst:207
msgid ""
"``ppi`` is ``0`` for a display that does not say how large it is, as a virtual one in a remote "
"session or a virtual machine does not. Window systems assume 96 or 72 to the inch for such a "
"display, which is a guess and is not passed on."
msgstr "不提供物理尺寸的显示器（例如远程会话或虚拟机中的虚拟显示器），其 ``ppi`` 为 ``0``。窗口系统可能假定每英寸 96 或 72 像素，但这是猜测，不会转发给程序。"


msgid "A comma-separated list of preferred language tags from the terminal host, with the primary language first. macOS may report more than one tag, such as ``en-US,fr-CA``. Linux reports one tag from the user's account preference or the system or session locale. ``und`` means undetermined. The value follows changes as the OS exposes them to the running terminal."
msgstr "运行终端的主机的语言偏好，以逗号分隔，首选语言排在第一位。macOS 可报告多个语言标签，例如 ``en-US,fr-CA``。Linux 根据用户账户偏好、系统或会话区域设置报告一个标签。``und`` 表示未知。操作系统向正在运行的终端提供变化时，报告也会更新。"
